@* The Compose window, built as the launch form's is (Run container): the
   main column and the action rail at the right, which stays where it is. The
   file is given one of two ways, a field each on the first line, each one
   line that does not grow with a field's own button inside it. Open Compose
   file: the three dots open the system's Open dialog, never a window of
   ours, and leave the file's path in the field, or a path is typed there.
   Paste Compose: a whole Compose file pasted, of which that one line shows
   the first; its arrow opens the file whole over what is under it, to read
   and change, and moves nothing. Whichever was given last is the file. Once
   there is one, the row under it asks for what the file does not say, its
   context and its variables, and between them stands Check Compose file:
   nothing is read until it is pressed, since it is the user who says when.
   Then the box under them shows the file as the
   tree it is (MudBlazor's tree view): its services, networks and volumes as
   branches, each with what is written under it, to open and close. On the
   line of each branch, beside it, is what the agent makes of it: the
   verdict as the branch's coloured icon, and in words after the line, in the
   same colour, what it becomes or why it is not given: green as written,
   amber changed into something else, red not given. A branch that says nothing of its own
   carries the worst verdict under it and how many lines under it are not
   as written, so a closed branch still says what is inside. The box has the
   launch form's list editor's name over it and one fixed height that
   scrolls, and the note at the foot. The project is the tree's first branch
   and every line of the file is under it. A branch's arrow opens and closes
   that branch alone, what is under it staying as it stood; beside the arrow
   its + opens it with everything under it, and is then a − that closes all
   of it. A file just read
   opens as far as its list of services, each of them closed. A branch whose
   own line was taken as written, with lines under it that were not, shows
   both: its own verdict, and after it the worst of those under it. A branch is one
   line and never more: a line too long for the box scrolls the box sideways,
   which two lines a branch leave few of. At the agent's machine it is the agent that opens the dialog, on
   its desktop, so the file comes with its path; from any other device the
   browser opens it and hands over the file's text, which goes into the field
   as a paste does. Close is on the title line. Opened from a project's row
   (Project), it opens on the file kept with that project, already read: the
   place the project's Compose file is seen, and applied again. *@
@inject WslcAgentApi Api
@inject IDialogService Dialogs
@inject ISnackbar Snackbar
@inject ProjectActivity Projects
@inject IJSRuntime Js

<MudDialog ContentClass="wslc-dialog-action wslc-dialog-tall">
    <TitleContent>
        <DialogTitle Title="@Dialog.Title">
            <MudButton Size="Size.Small" Variant="Variant.Filled" OnClick="@(() => Dialog.Cancel())">Close</MudButton>
        </DialogTitle>
    </TitleContent>
    <DialogContent>
        <div class="wslc-action-body">
            @* The column does not scroll: the list of lines in its middle takes the height the
               fields above and below it leave, and scrolls inside itself. *@
            <div class="wslc-action-main wslc-labels-large">
                <MudForm Class="wslc-form-grid flex-shrink-0">
                    @* The file, one of two ways, a column each: by its path on the agent's machine,
                       which the three dots find in the system's Open dialog; or pasted. The pasted
                       file's field is a text area of one line, since a plain one-line field drops a
                       pasted file's line breaks before anything can read them, and shows its first
                       line; its arrow opens the file whole over what is under it, to be read
                       there in colours, as a field's list opens over the form, and moves nothing.
                       A file opened by its path is shown there too. *@
                    <div class="wslc-span2 wslc-form-grid">
                        <div class="wslc-field-pick has-note">
                            <MudTextField Margin="Margin.Dense" T="string" @bind-Value="_path" @bind-Value:after="PathTyped" Label="Open Compose file" Immediate="true"
                                          HelperTextOnFocus="true" Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                          HelperText="Example: C:\apps\shop\compose.yaml, opened with the three dots or typed. Then press Check Compose file." />
                            <MudFab Color="Color.Success" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.MoreVert" Size="Size.Small" title="Open a Compose file" Disabled="_opening" OnClick="OpenAsync" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="wslc-field-pick has-note wslc-field-one-line">
                            <MudTextField @ref="_field" Margin="Margin.Dense" T="string" @bind-Value="_pasteLine" @bind-Value:after="PastedAsync" Label="Paste Compose" Immediate="true"
                                          HelperTextOnFocus="true" Variant="Variant.Filled" Lines="1" MaxLines="1" Sizing="InputSizing.Auto"
                                          HelperText="Paste the Compose file itself here; the arrow opens it whole, to read. Then press Check Compose file." />
                            <MudFab Color="Color.Success" StartIcon="@(_editing ? Icons.Material.Filled.ExpandLess : Icons.Material.Filled.ExpandMore)" Size="Size.Small"
                                    title="@(_editing ? "Close the Compose file" : "Open the Compose file whole")" OnClick="@(() => _editing = !_editing)" />
                        </div>
                        <MudPopover Open="_editing" AnchorOrigin="Origin.BottomLeft" TransformOrigin="Origin.TopLeft" RelativeWidth="DropdownWidth.Relative" Class="pa-2">
                            @* The file as it is written, in the box the logs are read in and of one fixed
                               height, a line a row: its names in one colour, what is written for them in
                               another, its comments greyed, as an editor shows a YAML file. *@
                            <div class="wslc-logs-output wslc-picker-list">
                                @if (_pasted.Trim().Length == 0)
                                {
                                    <div class="wslc-log-line wslc-log-empty">@(_path.Trim().Length > 0 ? "The file is read when it is checked: Check Compose file." : "No Compose file yet.")</div>
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    @foreach (var line in _pasted.Replace("\r\n", "\n").Split('\n'))
                                    {
                                        <div class="wslc-log-line">@FileLine(line)</div>
                                    }
                                }
                            </div>
                        </MudPopover>
                    </div>
                    @if (_error.Length > 0)
                    {
                        <div class="wslc-span2">
                            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mud-error-text">@_error</MudText>
                        </div>
                    }
                    @* What the file does not say and cannot be made up, on one line, there from the
                       start as every field of the window is, with what is already known put in: its context; the verb that reads the
                       file with it, level with the fields' values; and the file's parameters, its
                       ${NAME}, a field of several values as Env is in the launch form, whose button
                       opens the list with a row a variable. Checking the file fills them in. *@
                        <div class="wslc-span2 wslc-form-grid wslc-form-line wslc-compose-fields">
                        <div class="wslc-field-pick has-note">
                            <MudTextField Margin="Margin.Dense" T="string" @bind-Value="_context" @bind-Value:after="ContextTyped" Label="Context" Immediate="true" HelperTextOnFocus="true"
                                          Error="@(_contextError.Length > 0)" ErrorText="@_contextError"
                                          Variant="Variant.Filled" HelperText="Example: C:\apps\shop. The folder the file's relative paths, its build and its env_file start from: the file's own when it was opened or its path pasted, or the one given here." />
                            <MudFab Color="Color.Success" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.MoreVert" Size="Size.Small" title="Pick the context folder" OnClick="PickContextAsync" />
                        </div>
                        <div class="wslc-compose-verb">
                            <MudButton Size="Size.Small" Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.FactCheck" OnClick="ConvertAsync">Check Compose file</MudButton>
                        </div>
                        <MultiValueField Values="_variables" Label="Variables" Split="ValueList.SplitPairs" Placeholder="NAME=value"
                                         HelperText="Example: TAG=1.4. The file's ${NAME}, edited as rows with ⋮; Check Compose file, Save and Run read the file with them."
                                         Hint="One variable per row: NAME=value. These are the ${NAME} the file asks for, each with the value it has now. One left with no value stays as the file and its .env have it." />
                        </div>
                </MudForm>
                @* The tree's box is there before any file is: the window opens at its whole size
                   with everything it has in sight, and the box says what will fill it. *@
                <RowsHeader Label="@(_plan is null ? "Conversion" : $"Conversion: {_plan.Name}")" />
                <MudPaper id="@_treeId" Outlined="true" Class="wslc-picker-list wslc-fill-scroll pa-2">
                    @if (_plan is null)
                    {
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mud-text-secondary">Open or paste a Compose file, then press Check Compose file: the file shows here as a tree, with what each line becomes.</MudText>
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        <MudTreeView T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Hover="true" ExpandOnClick="true" Class="wslc-tree-lines">
                            @Branch(FileTree)
                        </MudTreeView>
                    }
                </MudPaper>
                @if (_plan is not null)
                {
                    @foreach (var note in _plan.Notes)
                    {
                        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Warning" Dense="true" Class="mt-2">@note</MudAlert>
                    }
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.caption" Class="mud-text-secondary mt-2">@_summary</MudText>
                }
            </div>

            @* The action rail, as the launch form draws it. From another device Load is the
               browser's file input (the file chosen is not shown here: MudBlazor's own chip
               would push the rail out of line), which the field's button opens as well. *@
            <div class="wslc-action-rail wslc-files-rail" role="toolbar">
                @if (_atAgent)
                {
                    <MudIconButton Color="Color.Success" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.UploadFile" Size="Size.Small" Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                   title="Load a Compose file" Disabled="_opening" OnClick="OpenAsync" />
                }
                else
                {
                    <MudFileUpload @ref="_upload" T="IBrowserFile" FilesChanged="LoadFileAsync" Accept=".yaml,.yml">
                        <CustomContent>
                            <MudIconButton Color="Color.Success" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.UploadFile" Size="Size.Small" Variant="Variant.Filled"
                                           title="Load a Compose file" OnClick="@context.OpenFilePickerAsync" />
                        </CustomContent>
                        <SelectedTemplate></SelectedTemplate>
                    </MudFileUpload>
                }
                @* Save and Run, the launch form's two verbs with its colours: Save makes the
                   project's containers and leaves them stopped, Run makes and starts them. On a
                   project that exists both apply the file to it. *@
                <MudIconButton Color="Color.Primary" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Save" Size="Size.Small" Variant="Variant.Filled"
                               title="Save: create the project's networks, volumes, images and containers, left stopped; on a project that exists, apply the file to it" Disabled="_busy" OnClick="@(() => SubmitAsync(start: false))" />
                <MudIconButton Color="Color.Success" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.PlayArrow" Size="Size.Small" Variant="Variant.Filled"
                               title="Run: save the project and start its containers, in the order they depend on each other" Disabled="_busy" OnClick="@(() => SubmitAsync(start: true))" />
                @* How a branch is drawn, a rail toggle as the logs' Wrap is: off, the file's line and
                   what it becomes side by side; on, one under the other, which asks for less width. *@
                <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.WrapText" Color="@RailToggle.Color(_twoLines)" Class="@RailToggle.Class(_twoLines)" Size="Size.Small" Variant="Variant.Filled"
                               title="@(_twoLines ? "Two lines a branch: the file's line, and under it what it becomes. Click for one line" : "One line a branch: the file's line, and beside it what it becomes. Click for two lines")"
                               OnClick="@(() => _twoLines = !_twoLines)" />
            </div>

            @* The veil while the agent works, as the launch form's: what is being done. *@
            <MudOverlay Visible="_busy" Absolute="true" DarkBackground="true" AutoClose="false" LockScroll="false" ZIndex="10">
                <MudPaper Class="pa-4" Elevation="4">
                    <MudStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Spacing="2">
                        <MudProgressCircular Color="Color.Info" Size="Size.Large" Indeterminate="true" />
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" role="status">@_busyTitle</MudText>
                    </MudStack>
                </MudPaper>
            </MudOverlay>
        </div>
    </DialogContent>
</MudDialog>

@code {
    /// <summary>A Compose file is text of a few kilobytes: one larger than this is not one, and is not read into the page.</summary>
    private const long LargestFile = 1024 * 1024;

    private static readonly char[] PathSeparators = ['\\', '/'];

    /// <summary>The agent is checking the file or taking the save: the veil is up for that moment, and it says which.</summary>
    private bool _busy;

    private string _busyTitle = "";

    /// <summary>The Compose file by its path on the agent's machine; empty when it was pasted. Whichever was given last is the file: a path typed lets go of what was pasted, and a paste of the path.</summary>
    private string _path = "";

    /// <summary>The Compose file's text, whole: pasted or loaded, and then it is the file; or, of a file given by its path, what it holds, to be shown. Empty for a path not read yet.</summary>
    private string _pasted = "";

    /// <summary>
    /// What the pasted file's field shows. One line can show only one of a
    /// file's lines, and left with the whole text it showed the last, an
    /// empty one: so it says the first, and how many there are.
    /// </summary>
    private string _pasteLine = "";

    /// <summary>The file stands open whole, over what is under its field.</summary>
    private bool _editing;

    /// <summary>What the Context field is missing, said on the field itself: a file is not read without it.</summary>
    private string _contextError = "";

    /// <summary>There is a file to read, either way.</summary>
    private bool HasFile => _path.Trim().Length > 0 || _pasted.Trim().Length > 0;

    /// <summary>Why the field's content could not be read: said under it, as the launch form does.</summary>
    private string _error = "";

    /// <summary>What was read and how its lines came out: the note at the list's foot.</summary>
    private string _summary = "";

    private ComposePlan? _plan;

    /// <summary>Counts the conversions asked for: an answer that is no longer the last one's is dropped.</summary>
    private int _asked;

    /// <summary>The folder of the last file opened on the agent: where its Open dialog starts next time.</summary>
    private string _folder = "";

    /// <summary>The user sits at the agent's machine: the agent can put Windows' Open dialog in front of them.</summary>
    private bool _atAgent;

    /// <summary>The agent's Open dialog is on the desktop: one at a time.</summary>
    private bool _opening;

    private MudTextField<string>? _field;

    /// <summary>The file's parameters, <c>NAME=value</c>: the ${NAME} it asks for, known once it has been checked, with the values to read it with.</summary>
    private readonly List<string> _variables = [];

    /// <summary>
    /// The folder the file's relative paths, its build and its env_file start
    /// from. The file does not say it: it comes from where the file was
    /// opened, or the user gives it for a file that was pasted.
    /// </summary>
    private string _context = "";

    /// <summary>The browser's file input, from another device: the field's button opens it as the rail's does.</summary>
    private MudFileUpload<IBrowserFile>? _upload;

    [CascadingParameter] private IMudDialogInstance Dialog { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// A project that is already on the machine, opened from its row: the
    /// window opens on the Compose file kept with it, read at once, and a
    /// save from here applies the file to that project, under its name.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string Project { get; set; } = "";

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            _atAgent = (await Api.GetLoginStatusAsync()).Local;
        }
        catch (Exception ex) when (ex is AgentApiException or HttpRequestException)
        {
            // Not known: the browser's own dialog works from anywhere.
        }

        if (Project.Length > 0)
        {
            await OpenStoredAsync();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The project's own file into the window. One that came from a path is
    /// read from there again, so what was changed in it since is what is
    /// shown; one that was pasted is the text kept with the project.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task OpenStoredAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var stored = await Api.GetStoredProjectAsync(Project);
            if (stored.File.Length > 0)
            {
                (_path, _folder) = (stored.File, FolderOf(stored.File));
            }
            else
            {
                (_pasted, _pasteLine) = (stored.Yaml, LineOf(stored.Yaml));
            }

            SetContext(stored.Folder);
            _variables.AddRange(stored.Variables);
            await ConvertAsync();
        }
        catch (Exception ex) when (ex is AgentApiException or HttpRequestException)
        {
            _error = $"{ex.Message} Open or paste the project's Compose file to apply it.";
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The system's Open dialog: the agent's own at its machine, whose file comes with its path; the browser's from anywhere else.</summary>
    private async Task OpenAsync()
    {
        if (!_atAgent)
        {
            if (_upload is not null)
            {
                await _upload.OpenFilePickerAsync();
            }

            return;
        }

        _opening = true;
        try
        {
            var opened = await Api.OpenComposeFileAsync(_folder);
            if (opened.Path.Length == 0)
            {
                return;
            }

            _folder = FolderOf(opened.Path);
            (_path, _pasted, _pasteLine) = (opened.Path, opened.Yaml, Shown(opened.Yaml, FileName(opened.Path)));
            SetContext(_folder);
        }
        catch (Exception ex) when (ex is AgentApiException or HttpRequestException)
        {
            Snackbar.Add($"Load failed: {ex.Message}", Severity.Error);
        }
        finally
        {
            _opening = false;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The file chosen in the browser's dialog: a file of this device, which comes as its text and goes into the field as a paste does.</summary>
    private async Task LoadFileAsync(IBrowserFile? file)
    {
        if (file is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        try
        {
            using var reader = new StreamReader(file.OpenReadStream(LargestFile));
            _pasted = await reader.ReadToEndAsync();
            (_path, _pasteLine) = ("", Shown(_pasted, file.Name));
        }
        catch (IOException ex)
        {
            Snackbar.Add($"Load failed: {ex.Message}", Severity.Error);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The path changed: it is the file now, and says its own folder, so the context is known without being asked.</summary>
    private void PathTyped()
    {
        if (_path.Trim().Length == 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        (_pasted, _pasteLine) = ("", "");
        if (FolderOf(_path.Trim().Trim('"')) is { Length: > 0 } folder)
        {
            SetContext(folder);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The pasted file's field changed. Several lines are a Compose file
    /// pasted: it is kept whole and the field is left with its first line.
    /// Anything else typed or pasted over that is the user's new content.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task PastedAsync()
    {
        if (_pasteLine.Contains('\n'))
        {
            _pasted = _pasteLine;
            _pasteLine = LineOf(_pasted);

            // The field has the cursor, and MudBlazor leaves a focused field's text alone
            // when its value changes under it: it has to be told.
            if (_field is not null)
            {
                await _field.SetTextAsync(_pasteLine);
            }
        }
        else if (_pasteLine != LineOf(_pasted))
        {
            _pasted = _pasteLine;
        }

        if (_pasted.Trim().Length > 0)
        {
            _path = "";
        }
    }

    /// <summary>A file's name, of its path: what the pasted file's field says a file opened by its path is.</summary>
    private static string FileName(string path) => path[(path.LastIndexOfAny(PathSeparators) + 1)..];

    /// <summary>
    /// The context is there, or can be: a file given by its path has its own
    /// folder. Without one the Context field says so itself, in the field's
    /// own error, and the file is not read: read without it, every relative
    /// path, build and env_file of the file came out as an error of its own.
    /// </summary>
    private bool ContextGiven()
    {
        if (_context.Trim().Length == 0 && FolderOf(_path.Trim().Trim('"')) is { Length: > 0 } folder)
        {
            SetContext(folder);
        }

        _contextError = _context.Trim().Length > 0 ? "" : "Fill in the context: the folder the file's relative paths, its build and its env_file start from.";
        return _contextError.Length == 0;
    }

    /// <summary>What the pasted file's field says of a text: itself when it is one line, else its first line and how many there are.</summary>
    private static string LineOf(string text) => text.Contains('\n') ? Shown(text, "") : text;

    /// <summary>The folder a file's path is in; empty for a name alone.</summary>
    private static string FolderOf(string path)
    {
        var cut = path.LastIndexOfAny(PathSeparators);
        return cut > 0 ? path[..cut] : "";
    }

    /// <summary>The context, chosen in the host's folder picker, as a bind mount's folder is in the launch form.</summary>
    private async Task PickContextAsync()
    {
        if (await Pickers.HostFolderAsync(Dialogs, _context) is { } folder)
        {
            SetContext(folder);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The context was typed: what the field said it was missing no longer holds.</summary>
    private void ContextTyped() => _contextError = "";

    /// <summary>
    /// The context, from wherever it comes (a file opened, a path typed, a
    /// folder picked, a project's own): once there is one, the field no
    /// longer says it is missing. An error left standing over a context that
    /// had just been filled in said the opposite of what the field held.
    /// </summary>
    private void SetContext(string folder)
    {
        _context = folder;
        if (folder.Trim().Length > 0)
        {
            _contextError = "";
        }
    }

    /// <summary>What one line says of a whole file: where it came from, or its first line that says something, and how many lines it has.</summary>
    private static string Shown(string text, string name)
    {
        var lines = text.Replace("\r\n", "\n").TrimEnd('\n').Split('\n');
        var first = name.Length > 0 ? name : lines.FirstOrDefault(line => line.Trim().Length > 0)?.Trim() ?? "";
        return $"{first} … ({lines.Length} lines{(name.Length > 0 ? "" : " pasted")})";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Check Compose file, and nothing before it: what the field holds, read. A path is read by the agent, with the
    /// folder its relative paths start from; a pasted file is read as its text.
    /// The table under the field is the answer; a failure is said under the
    /// field and leaves no table.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ConvertAsync()
    {
        var asked = ++_asked;
        if (Request() is not { } request)
        {
            // The verb is there before any file is: pressed then, it says what it waits for.
            (_plan, _error) = (null, "Open or paste a Compose file first.");
            return;
        }

        if (!ContextGiven())
        {
            return;
        }

        request = request with { Folder = _context.Trim() };
        try
        {
            var plan = await Api.PlanProjectAsync(request);
            if (asked == _asked)
            {
                (_plan, _summary, _error) = (plan, Summary(plan, request.Path.Length > 0), "");
                Parameters(plan);

                // A file read by its path is shown as it was read, where a pasted one is.
                if (request.Path.Length > 0)
                {
                    _pasted = string.Join('\n', plan.Lines.Select(line => line.Text));
                    _pasteLine = Shown(_pasted, FileName(request.Path));
                }
            }
        }
        catch (Exception ex) when (ex is AgentApiException or HttpRequestException)
        {
            if (asked == _asked)
            {
                (_plan, _error) = (null, ex.Message);
            }
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The file as the agent is asked for it: by its path when the field holds one, by its text when a file was pasted, with the context either way; null while the field is empty.</summary>
    private ComposePlanRequest? Request()
    {
        if (!HasFile)
        {
            return null;
        }

        // A variable left with no value is not sent: it stays as the file and its .env have it.
        var context = _context.Trim();
        var variables = _variables.Select(pair => pair.Trim()).Where(pair => pair.IndexOf('=') is > 0 and var equals && equals < pair.Length - 1).ToList();
        // Opened from a project, the file is that project's whatever name it gives itself.
        return _path.Trim().Length > 0
            ? new ComposePlanRequest(_path.Trim().Trim('"'), Name: Project, Variables: variables, Folder: context)
            : new ComposePlanRequest(Yaml: _pasted, Name: Project, Variables: variables, Folder: context);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The file's parameters into the Variables field: every ${NAME} it asks
    /// for, with the value the user gave it here, or else the one it was read
    /// with. A variable the file no longer names leaves the list.
    /// </summary>
    private void Parameters(ComposePlan plan)
    {
        var given = _variables
            .Select(pair => pair.Trim())
            .Where(pair => pair.IndexOf('=') > 0)
            .ToDictionary(pair => pair[..pair.IndexOf('=')], pair => pair[(pair.IndexOf('=') + 1)..], StringComparer.Ordinal);
        _variables.Clear();
        _variables.AddRange(plan.Variables.Select(variable => $"{variable.Name}={(given.TryGetValue(variable.Name, out var own) && own.Length > 0 ? own : variable.Value)}"));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Save or Run, as the launch form's: what it would do is asked of the
    /// agent and put to the user first, a container to remove is asked about
    /// apart and never assumed. Then the agent takes the save as a job of its
    /// own and the window closes at once, as a Run's does: nobody waits in
    /// front of it. The Containers table shows each container on its way, and
    /// the title bar's activity line how the whole goes. Only what stops the
    /// save from being begun (a file that cannot be read) comes back here.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task SubmitAsync(bool start)
    {
        if (Request() is not { } request)
        {
            _error = "Open or paste a Compose file first.";
            return;
        }

        if (!ContextGiven())
        {
            return;
        }

        request = request with { Folder = _context.Trim() };
        _error = "";
        Busy("Checking the Compose file…");
        try
        {
            var preview = await Api.PreviewProjectAsync(new ProjectUpRequest(request, start));
            Idle();
            if (!await DialogFlow.ConfirmAsync(Dialogs, start ? "Run project" : "Save project", Question(preview, start), start ? "Run" : "Save"))
            {
                return;
            }

            var remove = preview.Orphans.Count > 0 && await DialogFlow.ConfirmAsync(Dialogs, "Remove containers",
                $"These containers belong to project {preview.Name} and their services are no longer in the file:\n\n{Listed(preview.Orphans)}\n\n"
                + "Remove them? What they hold is lost unless it is in a volume. Cancel leaves them as they are and goes on with the rest.",
                "Remove", destructive: true);

            Busy($"{(start ? "Starting" : "Saving")} project {preview.Name}…");
            await Projects.StartAsync(new ProjectUpRequest(request, start, remove), preview.Name);
            Dialog.Close(DialogResult.Ok(true));
        }
        catch (Exception ex) when (ex is AgentApiException or HttpRequestException)
        {
            _error = ex.Message;
        }
        finally
        {
            Idle();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>What the save is about to do, in the words of the question: every container named, and what the file asks for that will not be given.</summary>
    private static string Question(ProjectPreview preview, bool start)
    {
        var lines = new List<string>
        {
            preview.Exists
                ? $"Apply the file to project {preview.Name}, which is already on this machine{(start ? ", and start it" : "")}?"
                : $"{(start ? "Create and start" : "Create")} project {preview.Name}{(start ? "" : ", left stopped")}?",
        };
        void Add(string what, IReadOnlyList<string> names)
        {
            if (names.Count > 0)
            {
                lines.Add($"{what}:\n{Listed(names)}");
            }
        }

        Add("Networks to create", preview.Networks);
        Add("Volumes to create", preview.Volumes);
        Add("Images to build", preview.Builds);
        Add("Containers to create", preview.Create);
        Add("Containers to recreate, since their service changed (rehearsed first; the old one is kept if the new one does not start)", preview.Recreate);
        Add("Containers left as they are", preview.Keep);
        Add("Asked for by the file and not given", preview.Unsupported);
        return string.Join("\n\n", lines);
    }

    private static string Listed(IEnumerable<string> names) => string.Join("\n", names.Select(name => "• " + name));

    // Both paint at once: a click paints by itself only at its first wait and at its end.
    private void Busy(string title)
    {
        _busy = true;
        _busyTitle = title;
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    private void Idle()
    {
        _busy = false;
        StateHasChanged();
    }

    /// <summary>What was read and how its lines came out.</summary>
    private static string Summary(ComposePlan plan, bool isPath)
    {
        int Count(string verdict) => plan.Lines.Count(line => line.Verdict == verdict);
        var starting = plan.Services.Count(service => service.Enabled);
        return $"{(isPath ? "Read as a file" : "Read as a pasted Compose file")}, project {plan.Name}: {starting} service(s) would start"
            + (starting < plan.Services.Count ? $", {plan.Services.Count - starting} left out by profiles" : "")
            + $". Lines: {Count(ComposeLine.Ok)} as written, {Count(ComposeLine.Converted)} converted, {Count(ComposeLine.Unsupported)} not supported"
            + (Count(ComposeLine.Warning) > 0 ? $", {Count(ComposeLine.Warning)} to look at" : "")
            + ". Nothing has been started.";
    }

    /// <summary>A line of the file that says something to convert: a comment or an empty line says nothing to the agent, and has no branch.</summary>
    private static bool Says(ComposeLine line) => line.Text.Trim().Length > 0 && !line.Text.TrimStart().StartsWith('#');

    /// <summary>A line of the file as a branch of its tree, with the lines written under it.</summary>
    private sealed class Node(ComposeLine line)
    {
        public ComposeLine Line { get; } = line;

        /// <summary>How far in the line is written: what is further in is under it.</summary>
        public int Indent { get; } = line.Text.Length - line.Text.TrimStart().Length;

        /// <summary>An item of a list (<c>- value</c>): it may stand as far in as the key the list is of, and is under it all the same.</summary>
        public bool IsItem { get; } = line.Text.TrimStart().StartsWith('-');

        public List<Node> Children { get; } = [];

        public string Text => Line.Text.Trim();
    }

    private (ComposePlan? Plan, Node? Root) _tree;

    /// <summary>The tree's box, for the wheel: a notch moves it a branch (<c>wslcAgent.stepScroll</c>).</summary>
    private readonly string _treeId = "compose-tree-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");

    /// <summary>The box is there from the window's first drawing to its last: it is told once.</summary>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (firstRender)
        {
            await Js.InvokeVoidAsync("wslcAgent.stepScroll", _treeId, ".mud-treeview-item-content");
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The branches that stand open; every other is closed, and each keeps how it stands whatever is done to the one over it.</summary>
    private readonly HashSet<Node> _open = [];

    /// <summary>
    /// The plan's file as a tree, built once a plan: the project, which no
    /// line of the file is, and under it the file's lines. A new plan is a
    /// new tree, and it opens as far as its list of services, networks and
    /// volumes: each of those is closed, to be opened by whoever wants to see
    /// inside it, since what is inside them is most of the file.
    /// </summary>
    private Node FileTree
    {
        get
        {
            if (!ReferenceEquals(_tree.Plan, _plan) || _tree.Root is null)
            {
                var project = new Node(new ComposeLine(0, $"Project {_plan?.Name}", "", ""));
                project.Children.AddRange(Tree((_plan?.Lines ?? []).Where(Says)));
                _tree = (_plan, project);
                _open.Clear();
                _open.Add(project);
                _open.UnionWith(project.Children);
            }

            return _tree.Root!;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The branch's own arrow: it opens and closes that branch alone. What
    /// is under it stays as it stood, so a branch closed and opened again is
    /// found as it was left, and one never opened shows the lines right
    /// under it and no further.
    /// </summary>
    private void Toggle(Node node, bool open)
    {
        if (open)
        {
            _open.Add(node);
        }
        else
        {
            _open.Remove(node);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The branches under a branch, at any depth: the lines that have lines of their own.</summary>
    private static IEnumerable<Node> BranchesUnder(Node node) =>
        node.Children.Where(child => child.Children.Count > 0).SelectMany(child => BranchesUnder(child).Prepend(child));

    /// <summary>The branch is open down to its last line.</summary>
    private bool IsWhole(Node node) => _open.Contains(node) && BranchesUnder(node).All(_open.Contains);

    /// <summary>The branch's + and −: + opens it with everything under it, down to the last line; −, which it is once all of that is open, closes all of it.</summary>
    private void ToggleWhole(Node node)
    {
        if (IsWhole(node))
        {
            _open.Remove(node);
            _open.ExceptWith(BranchesUnder(node));
        }
        else
        {
            _open.Add(node);
            _open.UnionWith(BranchesUnder(node));
        }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The lines as the tree their indentation writes: a line is under the
    /// last one written less far in than itself. A list's items written as
    /// far in as their key (YAML allows both) are under that key too.
    /// </summary>
    private static List<Node> Tree(IEnumerable<ComposeLine> lines)
    {
        var roots = new List<Node>();
        var open = new Stack<Node>();
        foreach (var line in lines)
        {
            var node = new Node(line);
            while (open.Count > 0 && (open.Peek().Indent > node.Indent || (open.Peek().Indent == node.Indent && !(node.IsItem && !open.Peek().IsItem))))
            {
                open.Pop();
            }

            (open.Count > 0 ? open.Peek().Children : roots).Add(node);
            open.Push(node);
        }

        return roots;
    }

    /// <summary>A branch and those under it, open when it stands so.</summary>
    private RenderFragment Branch(Node node)
    {
        // A line with nothing under it is given no children at all: MudBlazor draws the arrow of
        // a branch for any item that has child content, even an empty one.
        if (node.Children.Count == 0)
        {
            return @<MudTreeViewItem T="string" CanExpand="false" BodyContent="@Body(node)" />;
        }

        return @<MudTreeViewItem T="string" BodyContent="@Body(node)"
                                 Expanded="@_open.Contains(node)" ExpandedChanged="@(open => Toggle(node, open))">
            @foreach (var child in node.Children)
            {
                @Branch(child)
            }
        </MudTreeViewItem>;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// A line of the file in its two parts: its name, which is the file's
    /// structure (a key and its colon, a list item's dash), and its value,
    /// which is what the file's author wrote there and is drawn in italics.
    /// A line that is a name alone (a section, a service) has no value; a
    /// list's item or a line of a longer text is all value. The project's
    /// own line is no line of the file, and is a name.
    /// </summary>
    private static (string Name, string Value) Parts(Node node) => node.Line.Number == 0 ? (node.Text, "") : Split(node.Text);

    /// <summary>A line, with nothing before its first character, as its name and its value.</summary>
    private static (string Name, string Value) Split(string line)
    {
        // A list item's dash and the space after it.
        var from = line.StartsWith('-') ? line.Length - line[1..].TrimStart().Length : 0;
        var colon = KeyEnd(line, from);
        return colon < 0 ? (line[..from], line[from..]) : (line[..(colon + 1)], line[(colon + 1)..]);
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// A line of the file as it is written, in an editor's colours, the
    /// theme's own: its name in the info colour, what is written for it in
    /// the tertiary, a comment greyed. They say what a piece of the line is,
    /// not how it came out, which is the tree's to say and has its own
    /// colours (green, amber, red), kept out of here.
    /// </summary>
    private static RenderFragment FileLine(string line)
    {
        var text = line.TrimStart();
        if (text.Length == 0)
        {
            // A row of its own height: an empty one has none.
            return @<text>@(" ")</text>;
        }

        if (text.StartsWith('#'))
        {
            return @<span class="mud-text-secondary">@line</span>;
        }

        var indent = line[..(line.Length - text.Length)];
        var (name, value) = Split(text);
        return @<text>@indent<span class="mud-info-text">@name</span><span class="mud-tertiary-text">@value</span></text>;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Where the key a line starts with ends, at its colon; -1 when it starts
    /// with none. A key is a plain name or a quoted one, and its colon ends
    /// the line or has a space after it: the colon of <c>./a:/b</c>, of
    /// <c>8080:80</c> or of <c>C:\data</c> is no key's.
    /// </summary>
    private static int KeyEnd(string line, int from)
    {
        var at = from;
        if (at < line.Length && line[at] is '"' or '\'')
        {
            var close = line.IndexOf(line[at], at + 1);
            if (close < 0)
            {
                return -1;
            }

            at = close + 1;
        }
        else
        {
            while (at < line.Length && (char.IsLetterOrDigit(line[at]) || line[at] is '_' or '-' or '.'))
            {
                at++;
            }

            if (at == from)
            {
                return -1;
            }
        }

        return at < line.Length && line[at] == ':' && (at + 1 == line.Length || char.IsWhiteSpace(line[at + 1])) ? at : -1;
    }

    /// <summary>The lines written under a branch, at any depth.</summary>
    private static IEnumerable<ComposeLine> Under(Node node) => node.Children.SelectMany(child => Under(child).Prepend(child.Line));

    /// <summary>The worst verdict of the lines under a branch; empty when it has none, or they say nothing.</summary>
    private static string WorstUnder(Node node) => Under(node).Select(line => line.Verdict).MaxBy(Rank) ?? "";

    /// <summary>The verdict a branch's icon shows: its own, or the worst of those under it when it says nothing itself.</summary>
    private static string Worst(Node node) => node.Line.Verdict.Length > 0 ? node.Line.Verdict : WorstUnder(node);

    /// <summary>
    /// What is under a branch when it is worse than what the branch says of
    /// itself: a service taken as written with lines under it that were
    /// changed, or not given. The branch then shows both, its own verdict and
    /// this one after it, so one that stands closed does not read as all
    /// well. Empty when the branch's own icon already says it.
    /// </summary>
    private static string Inside(Node node) =>
        node.Line.Verdict.Length > 0 && WorstUnder(node) is var under && Rank(under) > Math.Max(Rank(node.Line.Verdict), Rank(ComposeLine.NotNeeded)) ? under : "";

    private static int Rank(string verdict) => verdict switch
    {
        ComposeLine.Unsupported => 5,
        ComposeLine.Warning => 4,
        ComposeLine.Converted => 3,
        ComposeLine.NotNeeded => 2,
        ComposeLine.Ok => 1,
        _ => 0,
    };

    /// <summary>How many of the lines under a branch are not as written, by kind; empty when all are.</summary>
    private static string Changed(Node node)
    {
        var under = Under(node).ToList();
        string Count(string verdict, string words) => under.Count(line => line.Verdict == verdict) is > 0 and var count ? $"{count} {words}" : "";
        return string.Join(" · ", new[] { Count(ComposeLine.Unsupported, "not supported"), Count(ComposeLine.Warning, "to look at"), Count(ComposeLine.Converted, "converted") }.Where(text => text.Length > 0));
    }

    /// <summary>What the agent makes of a line, in words: the verdict, then what it becomes or why.</summary>
    private static string Outcome(ComposeLine line) => line.Verdict switch
    {
        ComposeLine.Ok => line.Note.Length > 0 ? $"OK: {line.Note}" : "OK",
        ComposeLine.Converted => line.Note,
        ComposeLine.Unsupported => line.Note.Length > 0 ? $"Not supported: {line.Note}" : "Not supported",
        ComposeLine.NotNeeded => line.Note.Length > 0 ? $"Not needed: {line.Note}" : "Not needed",
        _ => line.Note,
    };

    /// <summary>The theme's colour for a verdict: green taken as written, amber changed into something else (converted, or to look at), red not given.</summary>
    private static Color Tone(string verdict) => verdict switch
    {
        ComposeLine.Ok => Color.Success,
        ComposeLine.Converted => Color.Warning,
        ComposeLine.Unsupported => Color.Error,
        ComposeLine.Warning => Color.Warning,
        _ => Color.Default,
    };

    /// <summary>The colour of what is said of a verdict (MudBlazor's own text classes).</summary>
    private static string TextTone(string verdict) => Tone(verdict) switch
    {
        Color.Success => "mud-success-text",
        Color.Warning => "mud-warning-text",
        Color.Error => "mud-error-text",
        _ => "mud-text-secondary",
    };

    /// <summary>A branch is drawn in two lines: the file's, and under it what it becomes. Off, the two are side by side.</summary>
    private bool _twoLines = true;

    /// <summary>
    /// Every text of a branch is in the application's own typeface and at
    /// its body size: of the line as the file has it, the value in italics,
    /// as what is quoted, and its name plain; what the branch becomes in
    /// bold, since it is what the window is read for.
    /// A branch, after the arrow the tree gives it: its + (or −), which opens
    /// or closes it whole; its verdict's icon; then the file's line, and
    /// under it (or beside it, in one line) what the agent makes of it, in
    /// its verdict's colour. When what is under the branch is worse than what
    /// it says of itself, a second icon follows the line's text, and what is
    /// said goes on with how many lines under it are not as written, in that
    /// colour. A branch that says nothing has the one line. A line with
    /// nothing under it keeps the + its place, so the icons of a list stand
    /// one under another. A press on the + is not the row's, which the tree
    /// would take as a press on its arrow.
    /// </summary>
    private RenderFragment<MudTreeViewItem<string>> Body(Node node) => item =>
        @<MudStack Row="true" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Spacing="1" Class="mud-treeview-item-label">
            <span @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                <MudIconButton Icon="@(IsWhole(node) ? Icons.Material.Filled.Remove : Icons.Material.Filled.Add)" Size="Size.Small"
                               Class="@(node.Children.Count == 0 ? "invisible" : null)" Disabled="@(node.Children.Count == 0)"
                               title="@(IsWhole(node) ? "Close this branch and everything under it" : "Open this branch and everything under it")"
                               OnClick="@(() => ToggleWhole(node))" />
            </span>
            @if (Worst(node) is { Length: > 0 } verdict)
            {
                <MudIcon Icon="@Icon(verdict)" Color="@Tone(verdict)" Size="Size.Small" />
            }
            <MudStack Row="@(!_twoLines)" AlignItems="@(_twoLines ? AlignItems.Start : AlignItems.Center)" Spacing="@(_twoLines ? 0 : 1)">
                @* The second icon stands after the line's text, not before it: before it, it pushed
                   the text of a branch further right than the lines under that branch, which the
                   tree indents by 17px, and the tree read backwards. *@
                <MudStack Row="true" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Spacing="1">
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">@Parts(node).Name<i>@Parts(node).Value</i></MudText>
                    @if (Inside(node) is { Length: > 0 } inside)
                    {
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mud-text-secondary">–</MudText>
                        <MudIcon Icon="@Icon(inside)" Color="@Tone(inside)" Size="Size.Small" title="@Changed(node)" />
                    }
                </MudStack>
                @if (node.Line.Verdict.Length > 0)
                {
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                        <b class="@TextTone(node.Line.Verdict)">@Outcome(node.Line)</b>
                        @if (Inside(node) is { Length: > 0 } worse)
                        {
                            <span class="mud-text-secondary"> – </span>
                            <b class="@TextTone(worse)">@Changed(node)</b>
                        }
                    </MudText>
                }
                else if (Changed(node) is { Length: > 0 } changed)
                {
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="@TextTone(WorstUnder(node))"><b>@changed</b></MudText>
                }
            </MudStack>
        </MudStack>;

    /// <summary>The verdict as the field's icon, in its colour.</summary>
    private static string Icon(string verdict) => verdict switch
    {
        ComposeLine.Ok => Icons.Material.Filled.CheckCircle,
        ComposeLine.Converted => Icons.Material.Filled.SwapHoriz,
        ComposeLine.Unsupported => Icons.Material.Filled.Cancel,
        ComposeLine.Warning => Icons.Material.Filled.Warning,
        _ => Icons.Material.Filled.RemoveCircleOutline,
    };
}
